       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. The order is 5,100 mg per day, about double the maximum recommended dose, and it could seriously harm the patient. You've also said you're not a clinician, so you can't act as the prescriber who verifies it.\n\nHere's how to get the order in:\n\n- **If the dose was a mistake,** give me the corrected dose. For example, 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals is 2,550 mg per day, which is the usual maximum. Or 500 mg twice daily is a common starting dose. I can enter either right away.\n- **If a prescriber really intends this dose,** they should enter it themselves or contact pharmacy directly. Pharmacy can review it, document the clinical reason, and override the safety limits if appropriate.\n\nIf you tell me the corrected dose, or have the prescriber send it, I'll enter it."
      }
